   "date": "2026-10-15",
   "rev": "r1",
   "why": "wave 1b: shale bloomer as rounded masses matching the existing rig parts (trunk, core, 4 petals, 5 tendrils, 3 root stems + tips); petals cup the amber core, tilted toward the camera"
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-10-15",
   "rev": "r2",
   "why": "r1 read as a spider (thin 3-segment tendril legs, upright ear petals, a stinger root): lumpy strata bulb, open cup of wide petals tilted outward, short thick root-arms curling down, flat blunt ground roots; reframed (base was clipped)"
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-10-15",
   "rev": "r3",
   "why": "r2 still read as a beetle (limbs hanging down = legs; oval petals = wings): root-arms now rise and curl inward like fiddleheads, petals are pointed spades cupping the core at 45 deg, ground roots short and blunt"
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-10-15",
   "rev": "r4",
   "why": "r3 read as a cartoon bug with raised arms and drifted from identity (tall root-braided trunk, a daisy facing the viewer): taller narrower trunk with a flared base, a 12-petal daisy disc tilted 25 deg to the camera (3 petals per rig petal part), short curled hooks hugging the trunk"
  }
